Refactor main.tsx to be the central coordinator:
- Implement main layout with PhaseTracker on left, content area on right
- Route between phase components based on current phase state
- Handle automatic phase transitions based on game events
- Integrate all context providers (Phase, GameState)
- Maintain clean separation of concerns

Main app structure:
```tsx
function App() {
  return (
    <GameStateProvider>
      <PhaseProvider>
        <div className="flex h-screen">
          <PhaseTracker />
          <main className="flex-1 ml-48">
            <PhaseRouter />
          </main>
        </div>
      </PhaseProvider>
    </GameStateProvider>
  );
}

const PhaseRouter = () => {
  const { currentPhase } = usePhase();
  switch(currentPhase) {
    case 'combat': return <Combat />;
    case 'shop': return <Shop />;
    case 'death': return <Death />;
    case 'lab': return <Lab />;
  }
};
```

Implement transition logic in each component and phase manager:
- Combat → Shop: When all enemies defeated
- Combat → Death: When all player characters die
- Shop → Combat: When Continue button clicked
- Death → Lab: After timeout or button click
- Lab → Combat: When Start New Run clicked

Transition handlers:
```typescript
const usePhaseTransitions = () => {
  const { transitionToPhase } = usePhase();
  const { gameState } = useGameState();

  const handleCombatEnd = (result: 'victory' | 'defeat') => {
    if (result === 'victory') {
      transitionToPhase('shop');
    } else {
      transitionToPhase('death');
    }
  };

  const handleShopContinue = () => {
    transitionToPhase('combat');
  };

  // other transition handlers
};
```

Create GameLayout.tsx component to provide consistent layout structure:
- Extract layout logic from main.tsx into dedicated GameLayout component
- Position phase tracker (Run #, Round #) at the top of the screen, persistent across all phases
- Reserve fixed area at bottom left for control panel (development tools, reset buttons)
- Provide main content area that dynamically renders current phase component
- Use CSS Grid or Flexbox for responsive layout structure
- Ensure layout remains stable during phase transitions

GameLayout component structure:
```tsx
interface GameLayoutProps {
  children: React.ReactNode;
  currentPhase: GamePhase;
  runNumber: number;
  roundNumber: number;
}

export const GameLayout: React.FC<GameLayoutProps> = ({
  children,
  currentPhase,
  runNumber,
  roundNumber
}) => {
  return (
    <div className="h-screen grid grid-rows-[auto_1fr_auto]">
      {/* Top: Phase Tracker */}
      <header className="bg-gray-800 text-white p-4">
        <div className="flex justify-between items-center">
          <h1>Game Title</h1>
          <div className="text-lg font-semibold">
            Run #{runNumber} - Round #{roundNumber}
          </div>
        </div>
      </header>

      {/* Main Content Area */}
      <main className="flex-1 overflow-auto p-4">
        {children}
      </main>

      {/* Bottom Left: Control Panel Area */}
      <footer className="bg-gray-100 p-4">
        <div className="flex justify-start">
          <div className="control-panel-area">
            {/* Reserved space for control panel */}
          </div>
        </div>
      </footer>
    </div>
  );
};
```

Integration steps:
- Update main.tsx to use GameLayout wrapper around phase components
- Pass phase information and game state to layout component
- Ensure all phase components render properly within the main content area
- Maintain existing functionality while improving layout consistency

